  "text": "So, Em, dot, I was wondering, like, if we raise a small bridge round now before the Series A, does that, you know, send the wrong signal to investors? Not necessarily. A bridge can be fine if it's clearly for something specific, like extending runway to hit a near-term milestone that unlocks the A. The trouble is when it looks like a lifeline because things aren't on track. What matters is your story and your terms. If you frame it as buying time to increase valuation, many investors respect that.",
